  "caveats": [
    "The initial actual TCP matrix passed, but eight pre-election query tests errored because the constructor required a caller-selected campaign ballot. The corrected query snapshots the existing observed fence and needs no new grant. Original failed reports are retained.",
    "The intermediate 76-test build qualified discovery, activation, adoption and transport before STATUS routing was added to MembershipActivationEndpoint. The final 46-test build covers that endpoint integration and its actual TCP paths; the intermediate result is not relabelled as final-source validation.",
    "The actual original-bootstrap TCP matrix includes real activation and certified BARRIER publication at stable sizes 3/4/5. Joint/final adopted-store cases separately use conditional historical-observation fixtures and are not a complete distributed membership transition.",
    "A returned cut/ready flag is an unverified diagnostic hint. No peer directory, authority, promise, installation, vote, public read or READY derives from it. Permanent known identities are authenticated under the existing private-network crash-fault assumption.",
    "Historical proof provenance, newer complete-source acquisition/adoption, autonomous election, learners/joint completion, generalized voting/publication and complete distributed qualification remain open."
  ],
